WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.740
Which fan -favorite star can be spotted&nbsp;
in the background of the final episode of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.720
The Walking Dead? And how did they score the&nbsp;low-key cameo? Keep watching for the details.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:17.820
After 11 seasons and over 170 episodes, the&nbsp;iconic zombie drama based on the Image Comics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.080
series has reached the finish line. The&nbsp;
Walking Dead capped things off with a very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.960
eventful finale that even brought back several&nbsp;fan favorites, including Rick Grimes and Michonne.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.040
There was even a small cameo from Chandler&nbsp;Riggs that many viewers might have missed.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:37.620
Riggs played the son of Rick Grimes, Carl Grimes,&nbsp;for more than 100 episodes of the AMC series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.420
and during that time the character&nbsp;
had it pretty rough. Losing one's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.780
childhood to a post-apocalyptic&nbsp;
undead nightmare is one thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:51.300
but losing a mother and then an eye only&nbsp;
adds to the punishment the poor kid endured.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:56.040
Despite surviving all of that, he was not able&nbsp;
to survive long enough to make it to the show's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:01.500
final entry. Out of all the character endings on&nbsp;
The Walking Dead, Carl Grimes' death was arguably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:07.080
one of the most outrageous moments on the show,&nbsp;and it didn't necessarily go over great with fans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:12.311
The character's final appearance was in Season 8,&nbsp;Episode 9, and he has not been on the show since.

00:01:12.311 --> 00:01:13.320
"You okay?"

00:01:15.069 --> 00:01:17.580
"I don't want you to be sad after this."

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.440
But the talented people in charge of the show&nbsp;took advantage of an unexpected opportunity to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:26.340
make sure the actor who played the legacy&nbsp;
character entered the frame one last time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:31.320
While Carl Grimes is long gone, Chandler Riggs&nbsp;managed to make it into the final episode of The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:36.180
Walking Dead. Toward the end of Season 11,&nbsp;Episode 24, there is a scene at the Hilltop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:41.400
community where Daryl Dixon and Carol Peletier are&nbsp;talking to Maggie Rhee about what happens next.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.840
In the background of that ordeal, there are&nbsp;several people working and doing farming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:52.020
activities, including an individual standing way&nbsp;in the back who looks suspiciously like a two-eyed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.360
Carl Grimes. That's because it was Chandler Riggs&nbsp;playing a hilltop farmer in the background of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:01.740
series finale. While you might think this&nbsp;
move was a carefully calculated endeavor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:06.480
that is simply not the case. It turns out it was&nbsp;all by chance. The actor was visiting the set,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:11.160
and when they needed extras, he was chosen by&nbsp;the director Greg Nicotero, and Riggs did not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:15.780
hesitate at the opportunity to get back into&nbsp;
The Walking Dead. He told Entertainment Weekly,

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.560
"Aunt Maggie!"

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:32.244
"Hey!"

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.780
Nicotero also revealed to Entertainment&nbsp;
Weekly that Riggs didn't visit with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:41.100
makeup or wardrobe departments and that he went&nbsp;to work in the clothes he was already in, saying,

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.800
Norman Reedus was thrilled to&nbsp;
have his young co-star on set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.700
and mentioned that he tried to let&nbsp;
the viewers in on the secret, saying,

00:03:05.259 --> 00:03:07.479
"It's not like we're never&nbsp;
going to see each other again."

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.140
Maggie herself, Lauren Cohan, was also excited&nbsp;
to have Riggs back, telling Entertainment Weekly,

00:03:19.375 --> 00:03:21.955
While it was brief and somewhat out of sight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.955 --> 00:03:26.160
having Carl Grimes in the mix is a&nbsp;
fun little easter egg that fans will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:31.740
appreciate. But it does feel safe to assume&nbsp;
that Riggs' series finale cameo could easily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:36.000
make the list of Walking Dead cameos fans&nbsp;
probably missed the first time around.
 

